# Graph Implementation Patterns

## Cross-language edge types

| Edge kind | From | To | Join key |
|---|---|---|---|
| `gql_resolves` | TS `useQuery` call | GQL schema query field | Operation/field name |
| `gql_resolves` | Java `@DgsQuery` method | GQL schema query field | Method name = field name |
| `rest_match` | TS `fetch`/`axios` call | Java `@GetMapping` handler | URL path string |
| `type_match` | GQL type | Java `@Entity` class | Type name |
| `injects` | Class with `@Autowired` field | `@Service`/`@Component` impl | Interface type name |
| `calls` | Any function/method | Target function/method | Resolved symbol name |
| `imports` | File-level | Exported symbol | Import path resolution |
| `extends`/`implements` | Subclass | Superclass/interface | Class name |
| `renders` | JSX element | React component definition | Component name |

## Extractor enhancement rules

- When adding extraction to `typescript-extractor.ts` or `java-extractor.ts`, the existing `ExtractedSymbol` and `ScannedFile` types must stay backward-compatible
- New symbol kinds (e.g., `gql-operation`, `api-call`) must be added to the `SymbolKind` union in `source-scanner/types.ts`
- New data that doesn't fit `ExtractedSymbol` goes into dedicated tables (`graphql_resolvers`, `graphql_operations`, `rest_endpoints`)

## GraphStore conventions

- All graph writes happen inside transactions
- Use `ON CONFLICT` / upsert for idempotent ingestion
- FTS5 `nodes_fts` table must be kept in sync via triggers or explicit insert/delete
- File-level cascade: deleting a file row cascades to its nodes, which cascade to edges
